# `'wasm-unsafe-eval'` is there for Pagefind, which instantiates WebAssembly for the search
# index. It is the narrow WASM-only allowance — deliberately NOT `'unsafe-eval'`, which would
# also re-open eval() and new Function() to script. Without it Pagefind throws a CompileError
# and search silently does nothing.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-XSS-Protection: 0
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

# The Markdown mirrors (see /llms.txt) are NOT covered by a `/*.md` wildcard here: when two
# rules match one path, Pages *appends* their values rather than letting the specific one win,
# so a wildcard plus the /.well-known/agent-skills/*/SKILL.md rule below produced a spliced
# `Content-Type: text/plain…, text/markdown…`. src/build.ts emits one explicit rule per mirror
# instead, from the same list that generates the mirrors themselves.

/llms.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/llms-full.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

# Article feeds (generated by src/posts.ts). EN: Pinterest auto-publish + the footer link.
# RU: the footer link on /ru/ pages and any RU consumer that imports a feed.
# One rule per path on purpose — overlapping _headers rules CONCATENATE their values, so a
# /*rss.xml wildcard next to a specific rule would splice two content types into one header.
/rss.xml
  Content-Type: application/rss+xml; charset=utf-8

/ru/rss.xml
  Content-Type: application/rss+xml; charset=utf-8

# Bluesky domain-handle verification (atproto HTTP method): the body is our DID, served as
# plain text so a resolver reads the string rather than downloading it. Specific path, no
# overlap with the rules around it. Serving this = the handle @spintax.net is ours.
/.well-known/atproto-did
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

# Domain proof for the official MCP registry (HTTP auth method): the body is
# `v=MCPv1; k=ed25519; p=<public key>`, checked by mcp-publisher when it signs a publish for
# the net.spintax namespace. Public by design — it is the public half of the pair. Chosen over
# the DNS TXT variant because that one needs a Zone.DNS:Edit token this project does not have.
# Delete this file only together with the registry listing; without it, re-publishing fails.
/.well-known/mcp-registry-auth
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

# API Catalog (RFC 9727): the one API this site has — the /mcp MCP server. Linkset per
# RFC 9264; the media type is what makes a bare 200 verifiable as a catalog. ADR 0006.
/.well-known/api-catalog
  Content-Type: application/linkset+json; charset=utf-8
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# Web Bot Auth key directory (draft-meunier-http-message-signatures-directory). keys[] is
# EMPTY on purpose: spintax.net operates no request-signing bots, and a present-but-empty
# directory is the honest form of that answer. Add keys only if we ever sign outbound
# agent traffic. ADR 0006.
/.well-known/http-message-signatures-directory
  Content-Type: application/http-message-signatures-directory+json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# Agent Skills artefacts. text/markdown is what the discovery index declares them to be.
/.well-known/agent-skills/*/SKILL.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json
  Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# Pagefind search index.
#
# [CRITICAL] Pages serves assets with max-age=14400, which is why every local /css and /js
# URL is content-hashed through bustAsset(). Pagefind's entry files are fetched by Pagefind
# itself, from fixed unhashed paths, so bustAsset() cannot reach them: after a redeploy a
# cached pagefind-entry.json can point at index shards that no longer exist, and search
# breaks for four hours with nothing failing on our side. Short max-age on the unhashed
# files, immutable on the content-hashed ones.
#
# Rules here must not overlap: matching _headers rules CONCATENATE their values rather than
# the specific one winning (that is how an invalid spliced Content-Type got shipped once).
# The pagefind-*-ui.* and pagefind-highlight.js bundles are omitted on purpose — we drive
# Pagefind through its headless API and never request them.

/pagefind/pagefind.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

/pagefind/pagefind-entry.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

/pagefind/pagefind-worker.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# Unhashed despite carrying the language in the name: a Pagefind version bump would
# otherwise pair a stale runtime with a fresh index.
/pagefind/wasm.*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

/pagefind/*.pf_meta
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/pagefind/index/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/pagefind/fragment/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
